f64521d4cea00283014038a", "scripts/tests/variant_fixtures.py": "73343b0880b0f8c81889873343123d5dd38dad207b5e99788eb5fe9e7881a553", "scripts/validate_skill.py": "28e44c912893e7224fab5a874e4fdd21c23fd4f57b5ce6c5ce9ff0cc33e9e61e", "scripts/variant_accept.py": "a4f7073f7250b9381d0ba01213134e268b3d30128e7119932766ec9590e3e58a", "scripts/variant_context.py": "eb3c208945d11a0e59eab6fa1e9d6958bdab774cb2301be38da0786d1027e9e8", "scripts/variant_draft.py": "7444f948e16378b3f9bf07f43269bcb1d0d2ea2dcb9ac0e0993dbe0ab424368c", "scripts/variant_plan.py": "de5fac1413e95185af09c053e31e8d7f1c38e6f466958d8985ba0a7bdc4d7ad5", "scripts/variant_review.py": "5c6293aab4c7e0d65d9b8e5c1789719d5cd41b6eefb774d84d3e60b58f7ef5fd", "scripts/variant_schema.py": "b0b5a794411c4c4858a29f35615dec36c69c6403ac103490f325ec2b3db86320", "tsconfig.json": "123412b493c51ecfb20cee097a963f2a6c57efb6b4aa422676275e88833b02f4"}, "factory_body": {"sha256": "1f218b2d9a9e39bed1d8842d95dea8f5fe9fb4ed7214cf6281576a468efa3614", "text": "---\nname: skill-factory\ndescription: \"Use when a workflow or capability must become a new agent skill, when an existing skill must be updated or standardized without losing its purpose, when a user-level or project-level variant is needed, or when a skill needs validation, evaluation, scaffolding, scripts, tests, or a Mise task graph.\"\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Kiren Srinivasan\n  version: \"0.5.1\"\n  scope: \"user\"\n---\n\n## Outcome\n\nProduce a complete, portable skill that accomplishes its declared result and proves that result under its actual conditions of use. Apply this contract to the factory and every skill it creates, updates, standardizes, imports, adapts, refreshes, invokes, checks or maintains. Include every instruction, reference, asset, schema, configuration, template, script, workflow, test, example, evaluation, integration and output. Preserve the intended purpose, accepted behavior, source bytes, authorized scope, independent variants, lineage and unrelated work. Keep all mandatory requirements conjunctive. A successful workflow, valid package or passing average cannot compensate for a missing capability or mandatory proof.\n\nRead this entire body first. It is the central owner of core behavior, the reusable ledger method and everything needed to understand the first decision. Budget context without removing required full reads. On the first loading and every successful later loading, the invoking agent must load the entire current governing ledger, all always-required rules and relationships, and the declared initial resources before dependent work. Resolve their actual paths, identities, public routes and consumers through the [use-case record][use-case], checked by `mise run use-case-policy`. Missing, stale, misrouted or ignored required content blocks its consumer. A reference, digest, receipt, earlier loading or acknowledgment does not prove that the current content was read and used. The invoking agent owns integration and final proof after any authorized delegation.\n\nResolve availability and audience before affected writes. This factory has `metadata.scope: \"user\"`. Every new or changed skill has exactly one scope string: `user` means availability across the user's projects; `project` means availability for one project or repository. The use-case record owns `audience.primary: human` or `agent`, according to who consumes the main result. Preserve valid designations and other valid metadata unless an authorized change or resolved purpose conflict requires otherwise. Record secondary and output-specific consumers where they change the contract. Scope, executor, report recipient, working directory, registry location and generic wording cannot substitute for the primary audience. Invalid values, types and duplicate keys fail. Untouched legacy inspection may allow missing designations; changed-output acceptance may not. Use `mise run resolve-scope` and the [scope contract](references/skill-scope-contract.md) for unresolved scope, then the supported host integration for authorized placement. Classification grants no installation, movement, duplication or permission authority.\n\n| Reading and action key | Required distinction before using the workflow |\n| --- | --- |\n| Main result | For a human result, examine what the person can do or experience. For an agent result, examine the actual next consumer and its usable input. A human-facing report does not change an agent primary result. An audience change adapts inputs, instructions, interfaces, presentation, evals and human participation; relabeling is insufficient. |\n| Scope | User and project describe intended availability. Adapt purpose and project assumptions when scope changes; moving a folder or changing a label does not prove suitability. |\n| Reading | The named reader loads current instructions, conditional guidance, data, examples, code or evidence according to their distinct authority and purpose. Then prove required use at the next consumer. For initial context, the use-case declaration owns `binding`. `package` (also the default) pins its contract-relative path and SHA-256. `invocation` declares the required ID, role and reading dependencies; the caller supplies the authorized path and current SHA-256. Request data cannot change the binding mode. Both forms require exact current bytes and full UTF-8 capture. Neither grants access authority nor accepts ledger meaning. |\n| Writing and acting | The authorized model or program writes the stated artifact; the effect owner performs the real operation. Mere planning, generated commands, process startup or a successful exit does not prove the intended effect. |\n| Judging | Models retain meaning, relevance, causal reasoning, perception and creative judgment. Humans retain their authentic decisions and assigned evidence. Neither a schema nor a workflow makes these judgments deterministic. |\n| Verifying and validating | Verification checks a stated property with a capable predicate or evaluator. Validation determines whether the integrated result serves the intended need in its actual context. Name the responsible acceptance owner and limits. |\n| Proof and handoff | Bind the claim to actual inputs, selected outputs, versions, authority, evidence contents and responsible judgment. Pass the necessary context and truthful status to the next owner; delivery alone is not consumption or acceptance. |\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe factory exists to turn intent into usable capability while making the reasons, actions and proof inspectable. Separate repeatable mechanics from substantive judgment so automation removes avoidable work without narrowing intelligence, creativity, craftsmanship, taste or available authorized modalities. Give every material requirement its protected outcome and the failure it prevents. Keep conditions and valid alternatives so an executor can adapt without defeating the purpose. A technically correct component can still be wrong for its task, recipient or integration.\n\nKeep one canonical meaning owner, stable term, default route and material decision per branch. Reuse accepted structures before adding code or dependencies. Remove demonstrated duplication, decorative sections, needless indirection and choices with no outcome difference. Simple means understandable and complete under the contract. Line counts, task counts, dependency counts, token savings and speed never justify lost meaning, context, safety, privacy, accessibility, authority, proof or domain complexity. Measure the whole accepted result, including retries, waits and recipient effort, rather than rewarding isolated activity. Choose algorithms, data structures, formats, batching and concurrency from measured access, mutation, queries, order, interoperability and lifetime; reuse native streaming, indexes and atomic replacement where their actual guarantees fit.\n\nPrevent WorkSlop: plausible output that fails its task or transfers unfinished reasoning, checking or repair to its recipient. Establish the real need and next action, complete the producer's work, verify claims and sources, make the result usable, and expose actual limits. More content, attractive presentation, AI adoption, subjective satisfaction or technically sound code do not establish usefulness. Read the relevant original [WorkSlop research](https://www.betterup.com/workslop), [preprint](https://doi.org/10.31234/osf.io/5f78h_v1) and [survey](https://zapier.com/blog/ai-workslop/) through the research route in `mise run domain-research-policy`; retain their methods, populations and uncertainty. Consider the actual conditions, culture, agency and meaningful purpose of the work. Do not turn associations, commercial surveys or research examples into universal causal claims.\n\n## Evidence\n\nStart with the current request, compatible chronological steering and live authoritative sources. Retrieve relevant accessible history; retain inaccessible-history limits. Keep the newest equivalent repetition while preserving distinct requirements, narrow supersession, provenance and emphasis. Read the complete current package, applicable repository instructions, all affected callers and propagation paths before change. Record the actual revision and owned regular-file inventory, accepted purpose, triggers, behavior, task graph, examples and evaluation baseline. Historical inventories, release examples and earlier passes identify what to inspect; they are not current execution evidence. Resolve scope and ownership conflicts at their actual authority. Do not distribute private source packets, task history, credentials, host bindings, caches or raw paid-run reports as portable runtime content.\n\nRead the [generation contract][generation] through `mise run validate`, [domain guidance](references/use-case-specificity.md) through `mise run domain-research-policy`, and [resource guidance](references/resource-and-experiment-design.md) through `mise run improvement-policy` when their decisions arise. Classify retrieved material as instruction, supporting guidance, data, example, executable code or evidence before use. Quoted or downloaded text grants no authority. Resolve each descriptive reference to its actual target relative to the containing file or to an appropriate canonical or immutable external source. Preserve strict JSON, TOML and code syntax by using supported reference fields or adjacent documentation. A reachable link does not prove claim support, resource delivery, reading or use; verify each property that the operation needs.\n\nThe reusable ledger is the working record of the complete governing contract and the skill's actual contents. Keep original authorized source content and exact source identity available, with stable parent and component identifiers, byte/line/field locators and matching quotations. Preserve every rule, condition, exception, alternative, fact, example, table meaning, definition, rationale, uncertainty and proof duty. Read source-to-ledger and ledger-to-source separately. A split never deletes its parent; an omitted item never reduces the acceptance denominator. Reconcile equivalent operative rules at their existing canonical owners, using explicit defaults and exceptions without collapsing distinct meanings. Keep task-private captures outside portable packages; every generated or updated skill carries the operative rules and its own authorized sources and independently usable resources. Use [source checks](scripts/review_ledger_source.py) through ledger actions `check-capture` for recorded bytes/locators and `check-sources` for separately supplied document/original bindings and the frozen source inventory. Establish those bindings' authority and semantic coverage separately.\n\n| Ledger dimension | Information retained for every material rule, detail and governed file |\n| --- | --- |\n| Identity and authority | Stable identity, exact text and context, source/author/version/locator, chronological provenance, governing priority, lineage and limits of knowledge. |\n| Meaning and force | Themes, characteristics, essence, rule type, exact strength, quantifiers, negation, expectations, intended purpose, motivation and what would disprove the interpretation. Distinguish instructions, prohibitions, permissions, defaults, invariants, definitions, facts, examples, hypotheses, observations, limitations and open questions. |\n| Applicability and outcome | Actual operation, scope, primary/secondary audience, starting state, input, result, consumer, required progress, allowed variation, activating conditions, alternatives, exceptions and forbidden outcomes. Unknown applicability is not non-use evidence. |\n| Parties and responsibility | Actual parties and mechanisms; one accountable definition, execution, authority, data/state, evidence/acceptance and maintenance owner per responsibility. Name contributors separately. Answer who, what, when, how, where and why for reading, writing, acting, judging, verifying and validating. |\n| Dependencies and resources | Logical, data, artifact, interface, schema, software/runtime, tool, service, environment, permission, human, temporal, spatial and other actual domain prerequisites; provider, consumer, scope, readiness, continuing validity, exclusivity, conflict, feedback and recovery. Record required versus preferred order. |\n| Software and state | Actual consumed release/artifact/API/configuration/platform/lock, inputs and selected intermediates, state owner/lifetime/transitions, baselines, restoration, deprecation, retirement, confidentiality, freshness and invalidation. Installation, activation, readiness, authority and suitability remain separate. |\n| Quality and work | Correctness, grounding, repeatability, intelligence, creativity, craft, judgment, taste, safety, privacy, accessibility, maintainability, scalability and relevant human outcomes; time, context, compute, memory, storage, network, cache, concurrency, cost and recipient effort. Preserve justified non-use rather than fabricated scores. |\n| Evidence and decision | Exact proposition, criterion, falsifier, actual command/evaluation, input/output/subject/dependency/evaluator bindings, artifact content and provenance, assigned mechanical/model/human judgment, uncertainty, disagreement, missing/conflicting evidence, status, failed attempt and legitimate recovery. |\n| Body and change | Each file's real functional role, rules and relationships, core versus triggered content, owning body clause, actual initial/conditional load route, affected callers/outputs/proof, exact write, reason, readbacks, contribution to the outcome and next eligible work. No extension or unchanged file is exempt. |\n| Propagation and delivery | Actual generation/copy/update/standardization/import/variant/refresh/maintenance owner, independent customization boundaries, canonical checker version, output resources and proof, accepted local/remote contents, discovery, invocation and recipient use. |\n\nRelationships have their own identities, typed ordered endpoints, source basis, direction, conditions, grouping, roles, multiplicity, responsible review and evidence state. Preserve multiple endpoints and repeated occurrences. Distinguish an asserted source interpretation from a tested effect; keep candidates, rejection and stale review explicit. Never infer independence from an absent edge, unconditional truth from reachability, or transitivity from a familiar label. Review the following relationship families and add a newly discovered distinct source-grounded relationship at the same definition owner before use. Changing a definition requires review of its affected occurrences and generated-relation owner; changing an inherited meaning invalidates affected dependent reviews unless an explicit unchanged override preserves their effective meaning.\n\n| Relationship family | Distinctions the ledger and every traversal preserve |\n| --- | --- |\n| Source and meaning | `part-of`, `contextualizes`, `defines`, `references`, `equivalent-under`, `distinct-from`, `refines`, `example-of`, `qualifies`, `excepts`, `contradicts`, `supersedes`, `preserves`. Preserve the exact parent, scope and authorized exception; similar words do not prove equivalence. |\n| Logic and purpose | `requires-all`, `requires-alternative`, `requires-exclusive-choice`, `conditional-on`, `forbids`, `permits`, `must-be-absent`, `motivates`, `advances`, `prevents`, `protects`, `tradeoff-with`, `reinforces`, `interacts-with`. A preferred route is not a prerequisite; neither a tradeoff nor an example waives a mandatory rule. |\n| Order and availability | `read-before`, `executes-before`, `gates-effect`, `gates-acceptance`, `remains-available`, `exclusive-access`, `feedback-to`, `parallel-with`. Keep reading/design, executable scheduling, protected effects and acceptance separate; preserve native conditions and versioned feedback. |\n| Owners and effects | `definition-owned-by`, `execution-owned-by`, `authorized-by`, `state-owned-by`, `accepted-by`, `maintained-by`, `reads`, `writes`, `consumes`, `produces`, `hands-off-to`, `bound-to`. Required responsibility and observed performance are different claims. |\n| Proof and revision | `proves`, `falsifies`, `calibrates`, `invalidates`, `recovers`, `restores`, `tests`, `compares-with`. Evidence establishes its particular claim under its conditions; a test's existence or a supplied verdict is not proof. |\n| Body and distribution | `generates`, `copies-from`, `adapts`, `independent-variant-of`, `refreshes`, `body-represents`, `change-reviews-body`, `initially-loads`, `conditionally-loads`, `delivers`. The source body represents its target subjects' core contract and routes detail. Matching copies can both be stale. |\n| Concepts and composition | `alias-of`, `broader-than`, `narrower-than`, `related-concept`, `identical-to`, `approximately-corresponds`, `causally-influences`, `higher-order-interaction`, `selected-from`. Separate taxonomy, exact/approximate identity, causal influence, workflow order and evidence. A pairwise projection cannot replace a joint interaction. |\n\nTraverse in dependency order; retain source order and chronology as provenance. Require exact source/detail views, effective facets, original relationships, bounded incoming/outgoing traces, file impacts and explicit finite selections. [ledger](scripts/review_ledger_workflow.ts) through `mise run ledger -- <request.json>` provides recorded subjects, context, asserted relationships, declared source/reading/task edges, reachability, finite candidates, work context and file impacts. Detail views expose parent/group/document/file and inherited owners' relationship context without changing endpoints or implying truth at children. Enumerate candidates lazily with exact counts, stable identities, order/repetition rules, explicit execution/scan budgets and continuation; disclose omissions or sampling. Work at the existing named record owner, record actual actions and judgment, then check bindings, applicability, conditions, affected dependents, evidence contents and recovery. Distinguish vocabulary, representation, evidence and executed-test coverage. Full reads, valid structure and current reviews cannot establish sound judgment or operational acceptance. Required traversal and source verification gate acceptance. Label historical observations; current records do not prove live state.\n\nDevelop around this body. Before an entire-body rewrite, finish source and ledger reconciliation and prove its read/work/check infrastructure; prepare the new body from all current contents, then validate its complete coverage, unique ownership and dependency order before subsequent skill-file work. For dependency-ordered creation before a target body exists, supply the already reviewed candidate through the guarded bootstrap path. Its review must bind the current ledger, unchanged source and exact candidate bytes; read the complete candidate and review before and after each individual write. An installed body or body alias disables that path. Initial review records remain declarations with full acceptance pending. For SKILL.md installation or replacement, use an explicit `body_revision` with a separately retained previous-body snapshot or declared absence and the candidate review. The prepared `new_file` supplies the candidate. Bind previous and candidate bytes to the current ledger and source; reject stale review, aliases and source/snapshot overlap. Read the actual installed body before replacement, the candidate after installation, and all governing inputs and retained review around the change. Preserve modes and independent edits. Review declarations do not authorize effects or establish semantic or human acceptance. For every individual added, changed or removed file, including repeat writes, read the whole actual ledger, current body and authorized governing goal/source documents before and after that write. Trace the change's functionality, all affected relationships, initial loading, body clause, consumers, proof and intended outcome. If it changes a core aspect, update its owning body clause and reference. Record the exact effect, readback, separate semantic judgment and evidence invalidation. Apply this to the factory and every generated or updated skill. Optimize these operations by parsing each required full read once, reusing verified unchanged analysis and traversing indexes; a batch, cache, prior digest or acknowledgment never substitutes for a mandated read.\n\nDiscover prerequisites backward from the promised usable outcome, its acceptance, real effects and actual consumers. Include instructions/knowledge, source facts and evidence, data and selected artifacts, meaning/schema/interface contracts, workflow/control, software packages and transitive behavior, tools/services/processes, environment/configuration, authority/privacy/security, human participation/judgment, time/lifetime, resources/exclusivity, quality and domain-specific dependencies. For each condition name the provider, consumer, actual required state, proof owner, activation, failure and recovery. Preserve conjunctions, supported alternatives, exclusive choices, absence conditions, continued availability and the exact point protected. Reconcile every existing/new file and every dependency inside Markdown, Mise, Mastra, scripts, packages and handoffs; filesystem order and import order alone are insufficient. Find cycles or contradictions without deleting real dependencies, and separate necessary partial order from a preferred schedule.\n\nClaim deterministic enforcement only for a precisely stated condition and computable predicate that preserves meaning; captured inputs and declared environment; verified selected-version mechanism/configuration; every relevant protected route before effect; current identity and necessary check/use protection; typed failure propagation; actual rejected attempt with non-effect; and successful recovery. State the exact accepted property and perimeter. A schema, graph or repeated check is not semantic proof, a transaction or tamper resistance. Use supported atomic identity, transactions, locks or isolation when the required guarantee needs them, and retain host limits. Invalid mandatory input must not become success through warnings, optional hooks, false predicates, swallowed exceptions, stale caches, callback failures, status translation or an alternate/retry/resume route. A missing required mechanism blocks the consumer; instructed model compliance cannot supply an absent software guarantee. The [file writer](scripts/review_ledger_write.py) through `mise run ledger` guards caller-scoped file creation/replacement; body changes require the explicit `body_revision` review; it accepts `bootstrap_body` with explicit `body` and `review` file bindings only before the target body exists; factory scaffold creation also uses this writer after a complete current plan, initial-body review and all per-file declarations pass. Other writers still require integration. For usage, load [the example](examples/example-ledger-write.md).\n\nScheduling decides what runs and when; invalidation decides whether an existing result remains valid. Capture dependencies discovered during execution before downstream acceptance and pause or restart at a valid boundary when needed. Bind variable work to the actual selected intermediate and its review, not merely the request or seed. A changed source, owner, output, selection, dependency, evaluator, environment, authority or approval stales affected dependents; preserve unrelated valid work and deliberate variant customizations. Recheck expiring conditions at use. Run independent eligible work under actual resource and ownership limits without duplicate effects or competing schedulers. A creative feedback loop uses successive versions, purposeful progress and bounded review, not a circular prerequisite or an unbounded retry.\n\nFor uncertain or creative work, distinguish known, provisional, discoverable and judgment-owned inputs. An unknown answer still has prerequisites, but the final idea is not a prerequisite of exploration. Use supported alternatives and methods that fit the uncertainty without inventing approvals, briefs, idea counts, scoring systems or research exhaustion. Mechanize preparation, faithful constraints, identity, permissions and handoffs; preserve model or human responsibility for interpretation, perception, causal reasoning, novelty, suitability, craft and taste. Retain several contract-valid outcomes and visible disagreement where justified. Inspect available authorized visual, audio, browser, tool and other modalities directly when required; do not replace them with text, hashes or simulated perception. Physical smell, taste, touch and measurements require actual authorized people or instruments when the claim needs them.\n\nResolve vague meaning through the existing use-case and decision owners: establish the real outcome/context and alternate interpretations; retrieve definitions and material facts; make observable requirements and fixed/bounded/open choices explicit; trace actors, objects, interfaces and state; assign methods, capable checks and residual judgment; test competing interpretations, falsifiers, failure and recovery; then bind the decision and propagate it. Retain purpose, source force, conditions, expected evidence, allowed variation, uncertainty, versions and invalidation in the compact record. Use relevant requirement, design, causal, formal or experimental methods for their actual contribution, not to populate another framework. Preserve mathematical limits: finite cases and interpretation review do not prove a universally unique meaning or deterministic judgment. Test domain-name substitution and domain-term removal for lost specificity rather than accepting generic profiles.\n\nFor every required quality, choose an observable property, capable evidence and responsible judgment that match the real outcome. Review correctness, grounding, repeatability, intelligence, creativity, craftsmanship, judgment, taste, usability, safety, accessibility, maintainability and scalability where applicable; retain other promised qualities. Distinguish fixed requirements, bounded choices and valuable open variation. Calibrate evaluators with known good/bad and held-out or independent cases; investigate disagreement and sensitivity. Preserve uncertainty and contextual judgment rather than a universal taste score, arbitrary winner or composite average. An inapplicability decision needs the exact source condition and concrete domain evidence; unknown, absent capability, cost, inconvenience or an unperformed test is unfinished work.\n\nThe human-study and human-work matrix is mandatory for this factory and every generated or updated skill, including agent primary audiences and machine-facing operations. The existing domain-research, use-case, decision and evaluation workflows must load and use relevant current selections through explicit public Mise parameters and the declared Mastra workflow. Assign definitions, reading, writing, selection, judgment, verification, validation, maintenance and acceptance to actual owners. Bind canonical versioned inventories/resources and their source identities, definitions, hierarchies, readable links, licenses, mappings, evidence, conflicts, unknowns and extensions. Keep large inventories at their resource owners; this body carries the governing method and required initial selections. Missing resources, ignored input, bypassed use or a fixed shortlist presented as complete coverage blocks factory/output acceptance.\n\nUse complementary complete applicable starting inventories: [OECD fields of research](https://www.oecd.org/content/dam/oecd/en/publications/reports/2015/10/frascati-manual-2015_g1g57dcb/9789264239012-en.pdf), [ILO ISCO occupations](https://isco.ilo.org/en/isco-08/), [UN ICATUS everyday activities](https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/time-use/icatus-2016/), the [O*NET content model](https://www.onetcenter.org/content.html) with [versioned data and attribution](https://www.onetcenter.org/database.html), and [NIST's human-centered AI use taxonomy](https://www.nist.gov/publications/ai-use-taxonomy-human-centered-approach). Research classifications do not enumerate every human mechanism; paid occupations do not cover all work; occupational population data do not predict an individual's abilities or preferences; current-resolving identifiers are not immutable snapshots. Retain complete declared hierarchies, unmapped items, overlap, interdisciplinary work, source-defined other categories and named sourced or unresolved extensions. No closed taxonomy proves all present or future fields are known.\n\nExtend discovery to relevant sensory, physiological, cognitive, learning, emotional, social, ergonomic, accessibility, linguistic, cultural, economic, organizational, artistic, ethical, historical and physical/material fields. Include research, teaching, communication, creation across media, planning, coordination, engineering, making, repair, care, service, culinary, civic, domestic, recreational and emerging activities. These are discovery prompts, not a requirement to activate every field. Identify the actual people, task, artifact/experience, purpose, medium, setting, abilities/access needs, expertise, language, culture and time horizon from authorized evidence. Do not infer individual preferences from demographic membership or collect sensitive data merely to fill the representation. Distinguish producer capability from recipient perception, comprehension, decision, task success, learning, comfort, aesthetics, emotion, trust, originality and longer-term effects.\n\nRepresent arbitrary finite unordered selections, ordered sequences, repetitions, groupings and higher-order interactions across study concepts, work activities, people/context, outcomes, choices, constraints, evidence and judgments. Preserve meaningful order and multiplicity. Use exact, alias, broader/narrower, related and approximate mappings with the distinctions in [SKOS](https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/); no RDF service is required. Symbolic selectors identify the versioned inventories, selection rule, grouping, ordering, conditions and explicit execution bounds. Every concrete member remains addressable without another schema. Keep parsing, captured identifier resolution, filtering, canonical serialization and enumeration reproducible, including comparator, locale, schema and source versions. Canonicalize only semantically unordered structures. Prefer supported standard combinatorial iterators and lazy records over stored cross-products or model calls per cell; measure their input-pool memory as well as output size. Representability grants no usefulness, truth, permission or tested status.\n\nUse the matrix to make actual choices: map the brief and challenge its first categories; pose the exact property-to-human-outcome question and label mechanisms as hypotheses; read relevant authoritative standards, reviews and original studies including counterevidence; connect each applicable finding to a concrete choice and transfer rationale; assign the mechanism, model and human duties with capable checks; then inspect and revise the actual artifact against the intended outcome. Record publication/revision, population, setting, task, medium, comparison, measures, effect, uncertainty and access limits where available. Distinguish normative standards, causal results, associations, theories, documented practice and inference. Freshness alone is not relevance; separately supported choices do not prove their combined effect. Refresh material gaps and changed selections without loading every global cell into every context.\n\nKeep mechanical predicates, research evidence, model assessment, authentic human evidence and physical observations distinct. Actual permission, personal preference, expert craft review, subjective comparison and observed task performance answer different questions. Relevant research supports bounded transfer, not guaranteed appreciation or measured improvement in this artifact. Ease can differ from learning; productive practice may serve the outcome. Novelty and diversity need their own assessment; one story experiment does not establish general creative uplift. More agents, reviewers or checkpoints do not prove better collaboration. Model judges need relevant held-out or authentic human comparison and bias/context checks before claiming to predict human evaluation. Predeclare suitable comparisons, participants, order, sample, measures and uncertainty for required human evidence; do not invent universal sample sizes. Missing required evidence stays unresolved through the authorized handoff. Optional unavailable studies permit only narrower truthful claims.\n\n## Mise task graph\n\nMise owns the public command surface, pinned environment and outer prerequisites. Mastra owns each delegated domain workflow and its supported control/state/recovery. Tested scripts perform repeatable leaves and exact predicates directly in that environment. Caller-controlled models own residual meaning, causal reasoning, research interpretation, perception and creative capability. Humans supply their assigned authentic evidence and decisions; the host owns identity, permission and supported communication. Inventory the actual actors, tools, external systems and governed resources before assigning duties. Keep one owner per scheduling, retry, cache, state, cleanup and protected effect. Put an explicit handoff between these owners; never recursively invoke competing Mise graphs from workflow steps. A mandatory Mastra workflow must execute the skill's actual capability, including the factory's own domain work, rather than wrapping bookkeeping or a generic proxy.\n\n| User command | Existing public route and protected result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `help` | Show this grammar and a one-line result for each command. Use `mise run validate` for the [complete help example](examples/example-help.md). |\n| `new <prompt>` | Resolve the name, description, scope, audience and destination, then `mise run new -- --name <name> --description \"<description>\" --scope <user-or-project> --dest <destination> --plan`. Review its exact rendered bytes and repeat the same flags with `--review <review.json>` in place of `--plan`. A scaffold is not an accepted skill. |\n| `update <path> <prompt>` | Freeze the source with `mise run plan-standardize -- <path>`, then perform the authorized smallest-owner change through its current public route and validate the complete target. Preserve domain purpose and accepted behavior. |\n| `standardize <path>` | Use `mise run plan-standardize -- <path>` and the source's supported standardization path. Standardization changes shape/execution while preserving capability and authorized customizations. |\n| `standardize-target <path> <profile>` | Run `mise run standardize-target -- <path> --profile <profile>` as a no-write plan. Review the accepted profile, exact baseline and changes before repeating with `--apply`. |\n| `import <source> <destination>` | Run `mise run audit-source-corpus -- <source>` and `mise run plan-standardize -- <source>`; classify and preserve the complete source before the supported separate-destination conversion. An import command in this grammar does not invent a missing script interface. |\n| `variant <source> <user-or-project>` | Use `mise run variant` with the [variant workflow][variants] for plan, candidate, review and acceptance. Both directions require actual adaptation and independent validation; refresh is explicit. |\n| `validate <path>` | `mise run validate-target -- <path>` checks the target. Use `--inspect-legacy` only for untouched legacy inspection; it cannot accept a changed output with missing required fields. |\n| `eval <path>` | `mise run eval-target -- <path>` checks the evaluation artifacts, then execute the actual declared cases through their supported runner. A schema checker has not run those cases. |\n| `refresh-registry-lineage <skill...>` | `mise run refresh-registry-lineage -- <skill...>` refreshes owned lineage only after accepted registry changes and current prerequisite proof. |\n| `doctor` | `mise run doctor` reports actual supported readiness and the exact missing prerequisite. Its checks establish only their stated predicates. |\n\nEach actual supported situation has one explicit default route, its genuine alternatives and failure branch. Resolve tool readiness, current public interfaces, explicit user choices and material domain fit from the actual host and owners; do not assume availability from a name, install, model claim or preference. Honor relevant established preferences; inference remains provisional and grants no installation, access, communication, storage or effect authority. Keep client/account/project/callable-tool bindings and preference resolution in the integration layer. Preserve every available authorized capability needed by the outcome, including direct visual/audio inspection, web research, browser/computer interaction, tool calls and multimodal creation. Block only the affected unsupported consumer. Mandatory tools remain mandatory under their conditions; one user's binding cannot become another skill's host assumption.\n\nPass long prompts and agentic inputs through `mise run agentic-request -- --request <file-or-dash> --runner <executable> --runner-args-json <array>`. The dispatcher first automatically captures its current SKILL.md as `body`, with path, digest and text. The actual caller selects executable authority and argument boundaries outside untrusted request data. Bind the completed use case, outcome, domain terms, prompt, SKILL.md dependencies and primitives to their current digests, domain role, contribution, relevance and proof. Validate file/stdin input and actual UTF-8 content snapshots in `body.text`, `use_case.text`, `skills[].text` and `context[].text`, then deliver the typed envelope over stdin without shell interpolation. Required ledger, matrix and other resources need explicit parameters and actual consumer use through the declared public/Mastra route. Text snapshots do not prove binary-media consumption or model understanding. Preserve non-text modalities through the real capable runner. Structure, bounded whole-phrase matching, digests, process exit and output schemas do not establish relevance, correct choices or domain success.\n\nFor each consumed package, tool, language, snippet or integration, define the skill-specific result and proof; inspect the consumed artifact/version, public API, configuration and relevant transitive behavior; derive the domain design; choose the smallest supported composition; implement its real interface with native tooling; exercise it; prove the result and seams; then propagate independent support and invalidate affected proof. At the existing decision owner, distinguish what the dependency supplies, what the skill implements and residual judgment. Specify material argument/return shapes, units, encoding, nullability, defaults, validation timing, errors, effects, state lifetime, concurrency, retries, cancellation and cleanup. Use current first-party documentation, releases/source, installed types/schema and runtime probes. Preserve working languages/APIs. Distinguish public contracts, examples, internals and unreleased changes; unavailable source needs authorized probes and stated limits. Upstream success is component evidence. Never invent an API, depend accidentally on internals, substitute engines, suppress failure or redefine the goal.\n\nFreeze compatible published versions during outcome work. Declare the actual runtime and exact package/tool pins, native package-manager manifests/locks, peer/transitive requirements and supported platform/ABI, configuration, environment, credentials and services. Run shared Python helpers in isolated uv environments bound to Mise\u2019s resolved Python path, without ancestor-project selection or uv interpreter downloads. Preserve domain-specific environments and reconcile customized runtime declarations. A Mise tool lock does not replace application dependency locking; installation does not prove import or behavior. Research unfamiliar languages through their official practice and native checks without adding unused toolchains. Distinguish stable packages from experimental or beta features; use a consequential optional feature only with actual need, authority, activation, compatibility, rejection/recovery evidence and a supported fallback. Store versions and capability/non-use decisions at their existing owners. Unavailable or unproved mandatory behavior is a blocker, not a replacement permission.\n\nEvery task declares dependencies, including an empty list for a true root, and reaches CI or a public operation. Preserve outer graph guards against cycles, diamonds, duplicate or redundant paths, disconnected/unknown tasks and nested Mise calls. These rules do not prohibit valid Mastra joins, conditional branches, parallel work or bounded feedback. Inspect all effective task sources, inherited/template configuration, aliases, patterns, embedded `run`/`run_windows` task references, arguments and environment. Sibling dependency-list order is not sequence. Sequential run entries differ from a parallel task group. `wait_for` waits for an already scheduled task; it does not schedule one. Post-task subtrees run only after their parent has started, including parent failure, and do not run when a failed prerequisite prevents that start. Post tasks provide neither rollback nor crash recovery. Preserve task-environment non-inheritance and the fact that an empty child `depends` list need not clear inherited template prerequisites; verify selected-release behavior with actual probes.\n\nMise task includes are not model-context delivery. Usage declarations are not proof of argument forwarding. Task freshness and artifact caching are separate; bypass both when fresh baseline evidence requires it. Cache only deterministic work with complete input, tool/version, environment and output bindings, including captured randomness where appropriate. Never cache live judgment, mutable remote state or side effects as fresh proof. Preserve selected-release locking, task isolation, context/resource, MCP and skills-sync limits; native locks are not arbitrary cross-file transactions, MCP declarations are not host approval and symlink synchronization is not an independent variant. Use the native owner where it meets the actual guarantee and a tested script only for a missing guarantee. Classify every current schema-derived Mise config/task/tool primitive in the [primitive catalog and dispositions](assets/mise-primitives.json) through `mise run mise-primitives-policy`; prove useful domain application, including a useful creative composition, or source-supported non-use rather than nominal feature use.\n\n| Required companion support | Actual boundary and conditions to preserve |\n| --- | --- |\n| Usage | Keep one authoritative argument definition for parsing, help, examples, completion and interface documentation. Use its supported Mise integration for explicit resources, roots, scope, variants and long-input stdin. Verify exporters and actual downstream forwarding for spaces, Unicode, empty values, repetition, quoting, shell characters and environment. Run supported spec lint/diff through Mise; grammar and effect metadata cannot establish implementation equivalence. |\n| Packslip | Use selected-release manifests, signatures, artifact identity/platform/resource metadata and consumer policy where distribution needs them. A native Mise backend may meet the install role without the separate CLI; actual manifest-generation/verification roles still need their supported mechanism. Verify signer identity/key policy, bytes, project/version, expiry, rollback/withdrawal and separately claimed provenance. Decoding is not verification. Support does not authorize signing/publication or artificial binary artifacts. |\n| fnox | Prefer its maintained CLI for scoped credential subprocesses through Mise; do not substitute an incomplete environment plugin. Bind provider/profile, required names, identity, scope, lease freshness and actual consumer readiness. Missing/expired/overbroad credentials block despite warning/skip behavior or ambient alternatives. Keep values, private keys, caches, proxy material and lease secrets outside portable output and persistent traces. Scoped proxy/placeholder protocols are not universal OS isolation. Cache, encrypted sync, activation and authentication retain separate limits and authority. |\n| Pitchfork | Use it only for genuinely required persistent processes; finite transformations stay finite Mise work. Bind project/worktree identity, executable, working directory, ports, dependencies, pinned environment, lifetime and platform. Readiness must meet the actual consumer condition, including all required probes even when native probes accept first success. Reuse only matching healthy instances. Preserve child termination, bounded retry/health, interruption and cleanup of owned processes while leaving unrelated services intact. Autostart, listeners, schedules and host activation need actual purpose and authority. |\n| hk | Reuse the existing language/domain checks with exact roots and file selection. Pin its Pkl imports to the selected release and use the built-in evaluator unless a needed feature justifies another declared evaluator. Inspect actual fix/check settings; force and prove read-only behavior when required, including an empty diff. Authorized fixes preserve staged, unstaged, untracked and unrelated work; file locks have a limited perimeter. Incremental checks do not replace whole-package or behavioral proof. Test per-directory Mise fallback and configuration-cache behavior. Installing the tool does not install hooks or agent-host integration. |\n\nAll five companions need current official feature/interface/source review and compatible supported versions; actual use stays conditional on its source-defined role. Reconcile their boundaries in the owning Mise tasks and Mastra workflow, not a new supervisor. Exact tools, lockfiles, configurations, test credentials and probes belong to each real package's declared environment. Tool support grants no global configuration, new service, credential access, signing, hooks, MCP, machine changes or variant synchronization. Use disposable, explicitly scoped resources for required tests and preserve unrelated state. Read back actual native behavior before relying on composition.\n\nThe required Mastra workflow must use compatible published artifacts and a declared managed runtime, minimal necessary TypeScript definitions/adapter and native dependency lock. Preserve existing script languages and direct leaf implementations. Inspect and map input/output/state/resume schemas, steps, composition, sequential/parallel/branch control, loops, suspension/resumption, persistence/snapshots/replay, observation, dynamic definitions, scheduling and supported engines. Optional feature non-use does not waive the workflow itself. Bind each meaningful step to real domain input, action, output, responsible judgment and failure/recovery. A one-node status wrapper that bypasses substantive workflow behavior does not establish the required capability, and extra Agent/provider infrastructure is unnecessary when the caller already supplies the runner.\n\nTest the selected Mastra engine rather than trusting guide wording. Resolve branching discrepancies with actual all-true behavior and explicit exclusive decisions when needed; do not hide a mandatory failed requirement in a false predicate. Validate real input/output/resume boundaries: types, schema conversion and declared outputs alone are insufficient. Acceptance checks must affect the returned domain result; caught completion-callback errors cannot be the only gate. A suspended or bailed step must return before its protected effect. Persistence, snapshots and replay require suitable supported storage and recovery policy; they do not prove crash safety or exactly-once effects. Replayed/resumed effects still need current operation, identity, input and authentic approval bindings. Inspect changed definitions, missing steps and invalid resumes instead of accepting engine success as domain success.\n\nDynamic beta workflows need faithful supported serialization and supplied-registry resolution; generated data cannot choose arbitrary executable authority. Schedules and workers depend on the selected live host, storage, transport and endpoint controls; optional engines are neither interchangeable nor uniformly production-ready. Keep secret handling outsid