ingle hyphens and match the directory. Non-registry names retain `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*$` at the generation owner. Descriptions are quoted, nonempty, at most 1024 characters, begin with `Use when`, and state applicability/search terms rather than the procedure. License defaults to MIT unless the user directs otherwise. Metadata values are strings; author is Kiren Srinivasan. New versions start at `\"0.1.0\"`; skills own versions independently. Preserve valid metadata and scope/audience. Optional compatibility is 1 to 500 characters; allowed-tools is a string with supported specification semantics. Parse YAML and reject duplicate keys, malformed fields and invalid types.\n\nThe body and its template stay below 200 lines and 100000 characters, in the seven H2 sections Outcome, Motivation, Evidence, Mise task graph, Steps, Assets and Evals. Other Markdown has at most 200 physical lines. Keep each wrappable paragraph or list item on one physical line with required blank lines; frontmatter, headings, tables and code blocks retain valid syntax. Keep core rules and initial context here; route optional detail with its precise trigger and backlink instead of hiding requirements for size. Every resource reference, including custom roots, names its owning public `mise run <task>` in the same block or enclosing section. Link actual implementation owners descriptively while executable instructions use public tasks. `mise run lint-writing` applies the [writing rules](references/writing-rules.md): result first, simple active language, one idea per sentence/topic, defined consistent terms and dependency order. Same-meaning human review must confirm clarity and completeness; lexical lint cannot replace it.\n\nAll code, tests, configurations, templates and embedded snippets follow every applicable goal/repository rule, including non-coding rules. Load the [code rules](references/code-rules.md) through `mise run lint-code`. Keep at most 200 code lines per file, 30 owned lines per func